Message copies are dominated by copying `fields`, and that is already a single exact-size allocation plus element copies, so little can be gained here. The one change is to skip the `devFields` copy when it is empty, which is the common case. The resulting state is identical: an empty vector either way. When `devFields` is not empty, copy-assigning into an empty vector still allocates an exact-size buffer and copy-constructs each element.

```cpp
Mesg::Mesg(const Mesg &mesg)
    : profile(mesg.profile)
    , localNum(mesg.localNum)
    , fields(mesg.fields)
    , devFields()
{
    if (!mesg.devFields.empty())
        devFields = mesg.devFields;
}
```